{"kind":"request","text":"Planner: review draft 3 of the proposed contract amendment \"carry passes are recorded\", notes/2026-10-04-carry-pass-amendment.md at 90b91f31 on request/test-overhead. This owes a review decision only: no Git artifact, no landing. It answers your review of draft 2 (794e6f86, plans/014): the changes you asked for in A and C, the qualifications on B, D, E and F, and your three decisions. All thirteen acceptance cases stay and two are added.\n\nA. No name becomes reserved: the new names are types of system event, an act is another type of entry, so a document that declares a kind called carry-started is as valid as before and R-DECL-2 does not change; the reservation of draft 2 is withdrawn. A caller requires a guarantee with requireLifecycle (--require-lifecycle 2), and a log whose lifecycle is lower fails lifecycle-below-required, so a resealed, downgraded log never meets it; the report gains a lifecycle field, and this is the log's lifecycle, not a report format version. A reader that does not know a recorded version stops there with lifecycle-unsupported. A landing's version is the version at its land act, for the Room and for verify: one admitted before the event stays under version 1 while it is still prepared after the upgrade.\n\nC. Attempts are recorded: the Room seals preparation-started {op, attempt} in the transaction that changes the operation's attempt, and prepared names its attempt, so the same commit built twice is two preparations. A pass starts when an evaluation starts, in one transaction with no await, and its number is stored as the operation's current pass. The seal guard is: current pass, current attempt, being prepared, same policy, no end. So an old worker seals nothing after a new evaluation of the same preparation, after a new attempt starts and before its integration is built, or after a restart. Every derived closing event is sealed in the transaction that takes ownership away, so the log shows closure where it happened.\n\nYour decisions are taken as given: three evaluations of a check in a pass, the first included, then the turn ends with readiness marked due; nothing rests on a no-tree pass; the attempt is public. B's full key, D's qualified closing rules, E's recovery by recorded purpose or kind including legacy threads after a v2 activation, and F's amendment of R-DECL-20 are written in. The cost paragraph is corrected. Two things are left open at the end: whether every evaluation needs a pass, and a preview's lifecycle version.","body":{"conditions":"(1) Draft 3 is accepted, changed or rejected, with reasons, for A and C and for the qualifications of B, D, E and F. (2) If accepted: it is numbered and placed, the two open items are decided, and adoption is recorded with the owners and the order of work. (3) If not: what remains.","no_git_artifact":"true","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}